# Allowlist for scripts/check_facsimile.py
#
# One entry per line: "<path>: <code> <key>", the key as the checker prints it
# in brackets. Only problems that are knowingly left open belong here, each
# explained by the comment above it. The checker reports entries that no
# longer match a problem, so remove an entry once its case is fixed.

# --- Not facsimile links ------------------------------------------------------
# Legacy merged edition of No. 3, not used by the website (see
# check_references.allow): it has no <facsimile>.
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: pointer #facs-p403
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: pointer #facsZone-music-example1
encodings/3/mattheson/comments_merged.xml: pointer #facsZone-p4-1
# The guidelines show the attribute with a placeholder value.
encodings/guidelines/guidelines_en.xml: pointer #[corresponding
encodings/guidelines/guidelines_en.xml: pointer zone
encodings/guidelines/guidelines_en.xml: pointer in
encodings/guidelines/guidelines_en.xml: pointer the
encodings/guidelines/guidelines_en.xml: pointer facsimile]

# --- Page breaks with a wrong @n or @source -------------------------------------
# The @facs of these page breaks point to the right page; their @n (or
# @source) is a transcription error, left as it is.
# No. 4, 1731: pp. 320 and 321 are given as 310 and 311; 1719: p. 123 as 287.
encodings/4/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=310 #facs-p382
encodings/4/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=311 #facs-p383
encodings/4/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=287 #facs-p297
# No. 8, 1719: the score is on pp. 138-141 (the first two misprinted 136-137);
# the page breaks give 136-139.
encodings/8/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=136 #facs-p312
encodings/8/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=137 #facs-p313
encodings/8/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=138 #facs-p314
encodings/8/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=139 #facs-p315
# No. 9, 1731: the second page break n="347" is p. 348.
encodings/9/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=347 #facs-p410
# No. 11, 1719: the score begins on p. 158, not 150.
encodings/11/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=150 #facs-p368
# No. 15, 1719: the score begins on p. 178, not 174.
encodings/15/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=174 #facs-p398
# No. 17, 1731: the second page break n="400" is p. 401.
encodings/17/mattheson/score.xml: pb-canvas n=400 #facs-p463
# Commentaries, 1731: No. 5, the first n="329" is p. 328; No. 6, the second
# n="334" is p. 335; No. 7, n="318" and "319" are pp. 338 and 339; No. 19, the
# second n="412" is p. 413.
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_de.xml: pb-canvas n=329 #facs-p390
encodings/6/mattheson/comments_de.xml: pb-canvas n=334 #facs-p397
encodings/7/mattheson/comments_de.xml: pb-canvas n=318 #facs-p400
encodings/7/mattheson/comments_de.xml: pb-canvas n=319 #facs-p401
encodings/19/mattheson/comments_de.xml: pb-canvas n=412 #facs-p475
# No. 1 and No. 9: a page break of the 1719 print has source="#secondEdition".
encodings/1/mattheson/score.xml: pb-source n=103 #facs-p277
encodings/9/mattheson/score.xml: pb-source n=145 #facs-p319

# --- Surfaces outside the Prob-Stück, kept as encoded -----------------------------
# The encoders listed one or two pages of the preceding piece; nothing points
# to these surfaces.
encodings/18/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: canvas-piece facs-p418
encodings/21/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: canvas-piece facs-p433
encodings/21/mattheson/comments_1st.xml: canvas-piece facs-p434
encodings/23/mattheson/comments_de.xml: canvas-piece facs-p490
encodings/23/mattheson/comments_de.xml: canvas-piece facs-p491

# --- Kept as they are ---------------------------------------------------------
# 10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml is the raw output of an automatic measure
# detector (Deep Optical Measure Detector, 2019) on pp. 356-359: 169 boxes for
# the 105 bars of the Marcello aria, some doubled or overlapping, numbered in
# the order found. No file points to it and the website does not use it; its
# zones were moved to the current images like all others.
encodings/10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml: zone-order zone_01DRXXBW7YKF0TYESVJM0R8JTJ
encodings/10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml: zone-order zone_01DRXXBW8654SAR7B05781WY08
encodings/10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml: zone-order zone_01DRXXBW888RKBRJSJFKJWECKJ
encodings/10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml: zone-order zone_01DRXXBW8TAMDBPC5YDT11W3V6
encodings/10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml: zone-order zone_01DRXXBW8V10PK9H6M3SVKP57Y
encodings/10/mattheson/measure_annotations.xml: zone-order zone_01DRXXBW98EGP1QZBQYAYWRXSH
# 5/mattheson/comments_en.xml keeps an early (2019) facsimile on local images
# (facsimile/bsb10598495_00410.svg.jpg to _00413, about 1000 px wide) that are
# not in the repository. Its zones are linked to bars and paragraphs by
# @corresp; nothing points to them and the website does not use them. Their
# pixel space cannot be recovered exactly (scaled like the 2019 BSB images
# they lie up to 100 px below the score's zones of the same bars).
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_en.xml: graphic (line 107)
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_en.xml: graphic (line 136)
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_en.xml: graphic (line 158)
encodings/5/mattheson/comments_en.xml: graphic (line 167)
# No. 8: zones p2-1 and p2-1-2 frame §. 2 of the commentary (pp. 344-345),
# which comments_de.xml does not transcribe.
encodings/8/mattheson/comments_de.xml: zone-unused facsZone-p2-1
encodings/8/mattheson/comments_de.xml: zone-unused facsZone-p2-1-2
# Music examples inside a paragraph that goes on on the next page: the example
# comes after the paragraph's last zone in the text. No. 18: example 1 in p6-1
# (pp. 408-409); No. 20: example 2, beside the end of p2-1 on p. 417.
encodings/18/mattheson/comments_de.xml: zone-order facsZone-music-example1
encodings/20/mattheson/comments_de.xml: zone-order facsZone-music-example2
